================================================================================================
MODEL vs MARKET -- Brier score on the same bucket-hours (lower is better)
================================================================================================
  sec.6 fair value : 0.1739
  market mid-quote : 0.0772   over 235,145 bucket-hours
  better calibrated: MARKET  (by 0.0967)

  The quote is a better forecast than the model at every probability bin.
  This is sec.9's honest prior confirmed rather than refuted: the observation
  is public and free, and the market already prices it. No recalibration of
  the model rescues a strategy that has to trade against a better forecast.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROBUSTNESS -- how the market's forecast is constructed
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The headline quote is (yes_ask.high + yes_bid.low)/2, the midpoint of the
  widest spread in the hour. That pair is sec.6's punitive FILL assumption,
  reused here to score the market. Rescored on the hour's CLOSING mid,
  over the 235,145 bucket-hours where both closes exist:
    sec.6 fair value                        : 0.1739
    market, widest-spread mid (headline)    : 0.0772
    market, closing mid                     : 0.0683
  The construction moves the market's Brier by 0.0089 (closing mid is better),
  against a model-versus-market gap of 0.0967. The choice of
  quote construction does not decide the comparison.

